       The  [1mscanf[22m()  family  of functions scans formatted input like [1msscanf[22m(3), but read from a [4mFILE[24m.  It is very difficult to use these functions correctly, and it is preferable to read entire lines with [1mfgets[22m(3) or [1mgetline[22m(3) and parse
       them later with [1msscanf[22m(3) or more specialized functions such as [1mstrtol[22m(3).

       The [1mscanf[22m() function reads input from the standard input stream [4mstdin[24m and [1mfscanf[22m() reads input from the stream pointer [4mstream[24m.

       The [1mvfscanf[22m() function is analogous to [1mvfprintf[22m(3) and reads input from the stream pointer [4mstream[24m using a variable argument list of pointers (see [1mstdarg[22m(3).  The [1mvscanf[22m() function is analogous to  [1mvprintf[22m(3)  and  reads  from  the
