[1mCAVEATS[0m
       These functions make it difficult to distinguish newlines from other white space.  This is especially problematic with line-buffered input, like the standard input stream.

       These functions can't report errors after the last non-suppressed conversion specification.

[1mBUGS[0m
       It is impossible to accurately know how many characters these functions have consumed from the input stream, since they only report the number of successful conversions.  For example, if the input is "123\n a", [4mscanf("%d[24m [4m%d",[24m  [4m&a,[0m
       [4m&b)[24m will consume the digits, the newline, and the space, but not the letter a.  This makes it difficult to recover from invalid input.

